gorithms library"},{"path":"algorithm/ranges","title":"Constrained algorithms (since C++20)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::sort","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Sorts the elements in the range [first, last) in non-descending order."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"first, last, r, comp, proj"},{"label":"Return value","note":"An iterator equal to last."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"𝓞(N·log(N)) comparisons and projections, where N = ranges::distance(first, last)."},{"label":"Possible implementation","note":"Note that typical implementations use Introsort. See also the implementation in MSVC STL and libstdc++."},{"label":"Notes","note":"std::sort uses std::iter_swap to swap elements, whereas ranges::sort instead uses ranges::iter_swap (which performs ADL for iter_swap, unlike std::iter_swap)"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"ranges::partial_sort","note":"sorts the first N elements of a range"},{"label":"ranges::stable_sort","note":"sorts a range of elements while preserving order between equal elements"},{"label":"ranges::partition","note":"divides a range of elements into two groups"},{"label":"sort","note":"sorts a range into ascending order"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":780,"codeBlockCount":3}
